  "count": 2,
  "rationale": "Deploy mfa:admin and mfa:dbadmin together. The first blocks authentication to DC and ADFS, preventing admin_dc and admin_adfs. The second then blocks authentication to DB, fileserver, and backup, even if CI secrets expose stolen_dbadmin. Thus no exfiltration technique is reachable. No single control suffices: mfa:admin leaves the CI-secrets route open; mfa:dbadmin can be bypassed through DC or ADFS administration; segmented can be bypassed by escalating an unpatched workstation or laptop; and any single patch or mfa:user leaves an attack route open."
